<section class="gs-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="gs-faq__inner">
    <div class="gs-faq__header fade-in">
      <span class="gs-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="gs-faq__title">Graffiti Shield window film — FAQ</h2>
      <p>Honest answers about Graffiti Shield anti-graffiti film in Philadelphia from specialists with over 16 years of installation experience.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="gs-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="gs-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="gs-faq__item gs-faq__item--open">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>What is Graffiti Shield and how does it work?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Graffiti Shield makes sacrificial protective films for glass, metal, and mirrors. The film absorbs vandalism — scratching, carving, acid etching — instead of the underlying surface. When the film is damaged, it peels away cleanly and a fresh sheet is installed, restoring the surface to like-new condition in minutes.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>How is Graffiti Shield different from standard safety window film?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Safety film is engineered to hold glass together on impact from a blow or blast. Graffiti Shield is engineered to be sacrificial — it absorbs scratches, etching, and chemical attack so the glass beneath never needs replacement. Both protect glass, but they address entirely different threats and are often installed together for complete protection.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>What surfaces can Graffiti Shield protect?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Graffiti Shield makes films for glass, mirrors, stainless steel, brushed aluminum, brushed gold metal finishes, and specialty substrates through their Custom Shield line. If a surface is targeted by vandals in Philadelphia, there is likely a Graffiti Shield product for it.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>How long does it take to replace a damaged Graffiti Shield film?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Most single-layer film replacements are completed within one to two hours depending on the number of panels. The Glass Shield Multi Layer system allows individual layer removal without full replacement, reducing restoration time even further for properties with frequent incidents.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>What is the Glass Shield Multi Layer system?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Glass Shield Multi Layer is a 4-layer system where each 4-mil clear film layer can be peeled away individually when damaged, without removing the remaining protective layers. A property facing repeated vandalism gets continuous protection without repeated full re-installation between incidents.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>Is Graffiti Shield film visible on the glass?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Glass Shield and Mirror Shield are optically clear — the film is not visible in normal use. Metal Shield films are available in finish-matched replicas (Stainless Steel, Brushed Aluminum, Brushed Gold) that accurately replicate the underlying material appearance in normal lighting and at normal viewing distances.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>Does Graffiti Shield film affect the appearance of my windows?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Glass Shield maintains full optical clarity and does not affect visible light transmission or the appearance of your glass. It is not a solar control or tinted film — it is a clear protective layer that is essentially invisible once installed.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>What is the warranty on Graffiti Shield products?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Graffiti Shield provides a limited manufacturer warranty covering film defects and performance. Our installation is additionally warranted for workmanship. Full warranty documentation is provided at the time of installation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>Can Graffiti Shield be installed on existing windows without replacing the glass?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Yes. Graffiti Shield films are applied directly to existing glass surfaces — no glass removal or replacement is needed. The installation is non-invasive and most Philadelphia commercial projects are completed within a single business day.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-faq__item">
        <div class="gs-faq__q"><span>How do I get Graffiti Shield installed in Philadelphia?</span><span class="gs-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="gs-faq__a"><p>Contact Window Film Philadelphia for a free site assessment. We will evaluate your glass, metal, and mirror surfaces, identify the highest-risk areas, and recommend the appropriate Graffiti Shield product for each location. We provide written specifications and a proposal before any work begins.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

